# [[.Name]]

A starter Goa / Goa-AI service created by `surla init`, with a starter
evaluator suite that `surla verify` can run against it.

## What is here

- `design/` declares the `[[.Name]]` service. `ask` (POST /ask) runs the
  `helper` agent on a question. `price` (GET /prices/{item}) returns an item's
  price in cents. The agent can call `price` through its `lookup_price` tool.
  `design/model.go` declares the C4 architecture model.
- `gen/` is generated by `goa gen [[.Module]]/design`. Never edit it.
- `internal/helper` is the agent's planner and `internal/service` implements the
  service.
- `cmd/[[.Name]]` serves the API. The agent runs in memory and sends every
  model call to a goa-ai model gateway given with `-model-gateway host:port`;
  the gateway holds the model provider and its API keys.
- `eval/` is a separate Go module: the starter evaluator suite. It runs the
  `[[.Name]]` binary in Surla's sandbox, serves a scripted model (not an LLM)
  through its own model gateway, asks "How much is tea?" and "How much is
  coffee?", and checks both the answer and that the agent called
  `lookup_price` and answered from that call's result.

The evaluator suite lives in this repository, so anyone who can read the code
can read its scenarios. Its `holdout` tag only hides that scenario's details
in the report view `surla verify -builder-view` prints; it is not a secret
test. Keep real holdout scenarios in an evaluator repository builders cannot
read.

## Next steps

```sh
git init && git add -A && git commit -m "Start [[.Name]] from surla init"
surla preview -dir .
surla verify \
  -candidate-repo . -candidate-commit "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" -binary [[.Name]]=./cmd/[[.Name]] \
  -suite-repo . -suite-commit "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" -suite-module eval -suite-command ./cmd/[[.Name]]-evals \
  -request-revision <request_revision> -work-dir "$(mktemp -d)/work" -report-dir reports
```

`<request_revision>` identifies the confirmed change request you are
verifying; any label works when you verify outside the Surla server.
